    "title": "Proceedings of the 19th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 6: Tutorial Abstracts) - ACL Anthology",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "![ACL Logo](https://aclanthology.org/images/acl-logo.svg) ACL Anthology ⟨1⟩\n  * About⟨2⟩\n    * Announcements⟨3⟩\n    * Communication channels⟨4⟩\n    * Related work⟨5⟩\n    * Copyright⟨6⟩\n    * * * *\n    * Credits⟨7⟩\n    * Volunteer⟨8⟩\n    * Development⟨9⟩\n    * Feedback⟨10⟩\n  * Using⟨2⟩\n    * Citing papers⟨11⟩\n    * Links in the Anthology⟨12⟩\n    * Data access⟨13⟩\n    * * * *\n    * All FAQs⟨14⟩\n    * * * *\n    * ###### Details\n    * Anthology identifiers⟨15⟩\n    * Names⟨16⟩\n    * ORCID iDs⟨17⟩\n    * DOIs⟨18⟩\n    * Verified authors⟨19⟩\n  * Contributions⟨2⟩\n    * Submissions⟨20⟩\n    * Corrections⟨21⟩\n    * Author pages⟨22⟩\n    * Attachments⟨23⟩\n  * GitHub⟨24⟩\n\n\n## Proceedings of the 19th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 6: Tutorial Abstracts)⟨25⟩\nChenghua Lin⟨26⟩, Aline Paes⟨27⟩, Rodrigo Wilkens⟨28⟩ (Editors)\n* * * \n\nAnthology ID:\n    2026.eacl-tutorials \n\nMonth:\n    March \n\nYear:\n    2026 \n\nAddress:\n    St. Julian's, Malta \n\nVenue:\n    EACL⟨29⟩ \n\nEvent:\n    19th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics⟨30⟩ \n\nSIG:\n\n\nPublisher:\n    Association for Computational Linguistics \n\nURL:\n    <https://aclanthology.org/2026.eacl-tutorials/> \n\nDOI:\n    10.18653/v1/2026.eacl-tutorials⟨31⟩ \n\nISBN:\n    979-8-89176-385-2 \n\nBib Export formats:\n     BibTeX⟨32⟩ MODS XML⟨33⟩ EndNote⟨34⟩ \n\nPDF:\n    <https://aclanthology.org/2026.eacl-tutorials.pdf>\nPDF (full) ⟨25⟩BibTeX ⟨32⟩Search⟨35⟩\n* * *\nShow all abstractsHide all abstracts\npdf ⟨36⟩bib ⟨37⟩\n**Proceedings of the 19th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 6: Tutorial Abstracts)⟨38⟩**  \nChenghua Lin⟨26⟩ | Aline Paes⟨27⟩ | Rodrigo Wilkens⟨28⟩\npdf ⟨39⟩bib ⟨40⟩abs\n**AI -assisted Scientific Discovery, Experimentation, Content Generation, and Evaluation⟨41⟩**  \nYufang Hou⟨42⟩ | Steffen Eger⟨43⟩ | Anne Lauscher⟨44⟩ | Wei Zhao⟨45⟩ | Yong Cao⟨46⟩\nThis tutorial provides an in-depth overview of recent advances in AI-assisted tools and models that support and enhance the scientific research process, spanning literature discovery, idea generation, multimodal content understanding and generation, text/table generation, and AI-supported peer review.\npdf ⟨47⟩bib ⟨48⟩abs\n**Cognitive Effects and Biases in Large Language Models⟨49⟩**  \nMarkus Schedl⟨50⟩ | Ralph Hertwig⟨51⟩ | Antonela Tommasel⟨52⟩ | Shahed Masoudian⟨53⟩\nThis tutorial bridges psychology and NLP to clarify cognitive effects and biases in large language models, compares methodological assumptions across disciplines, and discusses practical evaluation challenges and open research directions.\npdf ⟨54⟩bib ⟨55⟩abs\n**Encoding and Decoding Language in the Brain with Language Models⟨56⟩**  \nAnuja Negi⟨57⟩ | Mathis Lamarre⟨58⟩ | Christine Tseng⟨59⟩ | Subba Reddy Oota⟨60⟩\nThis tutorial introduces brain-language model alignment and recent advances in scaling, multilingual brain encoding, brain-informed fine-tuning, and brain decoding with language models, including semantic reconstruction from brain data.\npdf ⟨61⟩bib ⟨62⟩abs\n**Multimodal Large Language Models for Human- AI Interaction: Foundations, Agents, and Inclusive Applications⟨63⟩**  \nShafiq Joty⟨64⟩ | Enamul Hoque⟨65⟩ | Ahmed Masry⟨66⟩ | Spandana Gella⟨67⟩ | Samira Ebrahimi Kahou⟨68⟩\nThis tutorial presents foundations, agentic capabilities, and inclusive applications of multimodal large language models, covering architectures, multimodal alignment and reasoning, conversational GUI agents, accessibility, multilingual communication, and responsible deployment.\n![Creative Commons License](https://i.creativecommons.org/l/by/4.0/88x31.png)⟨69⟩ ACL materials are Copyright © 1963–2026 ACL; other materials are copyrighted by their respective copyright holders. Materials prior to 2016 here are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 International License⟨70⟩. Permission is granted to make copies for the purposes of teaching and research. Materials published in or after 2016 are licensed on a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License⟨71⟩.\nThe ACL Anthology is managed and built by the ACL Anthology team⟨7⟩ of volunteers.\n_Site last built on 22 July 2026 at 14:46 UTC withcommit 280e4ed⟨72⟩._\n",
